    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Reproduces the celebrated French-Wong / Bohigas-Flores result: embedding a random two-body interaction into the many-particle Fock space (the Two-Body Random Ensemble, TBRE) produces correlated many-body matrix elements whose density of states approaches a GAUSSIAN, not Wigner&#x27;s semicircle, unlike an ordinary GOE Hamiltonian of the same dimension built from independent entries.">

